From 4e9d759879d3a3e40088703c9f11a75e45cd60e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:07:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Material arrays: second review of lot L1

- Synchronizations targeted on one array (`synchronizeOnHost(a, s)`,
  `synchronizeOnHostForReading(a, s)`): the accessors, the rotated
  evaluators and the mean thermodynamic forces no longer copy the eleven
  arrays to read one.
- `getLinearizedOperators` synchronizes the arrays for reading when the
  operators are created.
- `integrate` and the evaluators report the exceptions of the
  synchronization instead of stopping the program;
  `PointWiseModel::computeNextState` still synchronizes its status
  between the processes after an exception.
- The rotated evaluators use `checkPointByPointLayout`, which now takes
  an error handler.
- Methods named after the rules of mfem-mgis (`readWrite`, `write`,
  `readWriteTangentOperatorBlocks`, `writeTangentOperatorBlocks`); the
  read-only contract of `getArray` documented (`GetData` is not
  tracked).
- CMake: the API of MGIS is checked by compiling a test; the installed
  configuration searches the CUDA toolkit used to build mfem-mgis
  (`CUDAToolkit_ROOT`, policy CMP0074); with MFEM compiled with HIP, the
  header of `MFEMFieldOperations` is not installed.
- Tests: point-wise model (the shrinkage is incremental: a value of the
  beginning of the step set on the host then on the device), rotation of
  the thermodynamic forces of an orthotropic behaviour and its refusal in
  the component by component layout, mean thermodynamic forces called
  directly, the accessors of the gradients and of the thermodynamic
  forces, the stored energies, the tangent operator blocks after update,
  empty arrays of a material without point, output files named after the
  device. Removing any targeted synchronization makes MaterialArraysTest
  fail on the debug device, and on the cuda device except for the mean
  forces; the synchronizations before the post-processings (redundant)
  and at the beginning of `solve` (PETSc path) are not detected.
